node_modules/
dist/
*.log
.DS_Store

# `npm pack` and `pnpm pack` leave the tarball in the repo root. It is a build
# output of `dist/`, which is already ignored, so committing one would ship a
# stale copy of an artefact the release workflow builds from source.
*.tgz

# Text this repo measures against and does not ship. `.tmp/corpus/` is ten
# Project Gutenberg EPUBs borrowed from another repository's fixtures, 29 MB of
# them, and the harness beside it reruns the English measurement in
# `docs/provenance.md`. Nothing in `pnpm check` reads any of it, which is the
# point: a measurement is recorded in the docs and in the comment above the rule
# it constrains, and the corpus that produced it is reproducible rather than
# committed. `.tmp/README.md` says how to refill the directory.
#
# **The leading dot is doing work beyond this file.** charcheck globs the
# filesystem rather than git and reads untracked files happily; what keeps it out
# of the corpus is that a dotted directory is only entered when a pattern names
# one. `charcheck.config.ts` says so where the globs are.
.tmp/
